<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cardiff</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cardiff is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bristol">Bristol</a> Channel at the mouth of the Taff. Its castle was built around 1093 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-fitzhamon">Robert Fitzhamon</a> inside a Roman fort and became the centre of the marcher lordship of Glamorgan. The town grew rapidly in the 19th century as the world's leading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> port and was made the capital of Wales in 1955.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cardiff.jpg" alt="Cardiff" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: grahamwell / Graham profile at Flickr website · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cardiff_Bay_WMC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
